backhand: add OsStr byte fallback for wasm32-unknown-unknown

backhand's unix_string modules only implement their OsStrExt/OsStringExt
traits under cfg(unix) and cfg(windows). wasm32-unknown-unknown is neither,
so the v3 and v4 readers fail to compile for the WASM target.

This patch adds a fallback implementation for any other target that uses the
opaque self-synchronizing OsStr encoding (as_encoded_bytes /
from_encoded_bytes_unchecked / from_encoded_bytes). On
wasm32-unknown-unknown that encoding is the identity byte representation
(std uses the byte-based os_str fallback on targets without a real OS
string type), so arbitrary squashfs name bytes round-trip exactly, matching
the unix implementation's behavior. On any hypothetical target where the
encoding were not identity, the implementation still never reads back
anything that was not produced through these same functions, so it remains
self-consistent.

Applies cleanly to backhand @ eccf81b6f599cb90245d7c9694e95ee6023cad06
(v0.25.3). Reportable upstream as a portability gap.

diff --git a/backhand/src/v3/unix_string.rs b/backhand/src/v3/unix_string.rs
index 3c5cd41..2f639ce 100644
--- a/backhand/src/v3/unix_string.rs
+++ b/backhand/src/v3/unix_string.rs
@@ -35,6 +35,25 @@ impl OsStrExt for OsStr {
     }
 }
 
+/// Fallback for targets without unix or Windows `OsStr` extensions (for
+/// example `wasm32-unknown-unknown`). Squashfs entry names are arbitrary bytes,
+/// so they are kept verbatim through the opaque self-synchronizing encoding
+/// used by `as_encoded_bytes`/`from_encoded_bytes_unchecked`.
+#[cfg(not(any(unix, windows)))]
+impl OsStrExt for OsStr {
+    fn as_bytes(&self) -> &[u8] {
+        self.as_encoded_bytes()
+    }
+
+    fn from_bytes(slice: &[u8]) -> &Self {
+        // SAFETY: every `OsStr` this library stores is produced through
+        // `from_bytes`/`from_vec` below and only ever read back through
+        // `as_encoded_bytes` or lossy display, so the encoded representation
+        // stays self-consistent.
+        unsafe { OsStr::from_encoded_bytes_unchecked(slice) }
+    }
+}
+
 pub trait OsStringExt {
     fn from_vec(vec: Vec<u8>) -> Self;
 }
@@ -52,3 +71,12 @@ impl OsStringExt for OsString {
         OsStr::from_bytes(vec.as_slice()).into()
     }
 }
+
+#[cfg(not(any(unix, windows)))]
+impl OsStringExt for OsString {
+    fn from_vec(vec: Vec<u8>) -> Self {
+        // SAFETY: see `OsStrExt::from_bytes` above; the byte representation is
+        // only ever produced and consumed inside this library.
+        unsafe { OsString::from_encoded_bytes_unchecked(vec) }
+    }
+}
